      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. it's a good start. the content is fine, but if i run this through the checker right now, the score is going to be pretty low because there aren't many structural elements. \n\nit's probably too \"flat\" for the tool to recognize it as a complete guide. can you expand this section to include the actual authentication request details? specifically, i need the header requirements for the POST request, the token lifecycle, and the error handling. \n\njust try to make it a bit more robust so the score picks it up, but seriously—don't go overboard. keep it meaningful.",
